{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["For only Og king of Bashan, etc. — therefore the Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: Fear him not." "Behold his bed — a cradle of a small child, from when he was an infant, in Old French 'berceau'." "A bed of iron — because when he was small he was very strong, and when he lay down he would break a bed of wood; therefore they made him one of iron, for a grown man who has understanding would not have needed this." "Is it not in Rabbat Benei Ammon — it still lies there in the place where he was raised in his childhood, as a marvel, that he was so large even in his childhood; but the bed of a grown man is not usually kept in one place, for he has beds in many places. And I have heard the following explanation of 'Is it not in Rabbat Benei Ammon': because he heard that Moshe was commanded by the mouth of the Almighty, 'Do not harass them nor contend with them' regarding Benei Ammon — for Israel were not permitted even angaria over Benei Ammon — and he knew that Israel would wage war against him, therefore he anticipated and placed his bed and his couch inside the city of Rabbat Benei Ammon, and it was a royal city, as is explained in the book of Samuel, so that Israel would not lay hold of his bed, for he knew they were not permitted to come there, from Abraham." "A true man — that he had reached his full growth."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :register {:flags {3 ["the Almighty"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:38:47.648136643Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}